# The analytic input of the ring half, in the form node N6 actually delivers

`Work.ORBridgeLinnell.HughesFreeInput` has two fields, and neither is produced by any delivered
node.  This file splits them off and states the *first* one in the form in which the JZLA20 engine
(Corollary 6.3, node N6) is available:

* `Work.ORFinal.DivLoc K G φK` — **(I4) of Jaikin-Zapirain--Linton in the form of the JZLA20
  engine**: for every *locally indicable* subgroup `H ≤ G`, the division closure `D H` of `K[H]` in
  `U(G)` is a division ring.  `Work.ORHughesFree.hughesFree_exists_locallyIndicable` is stated
  exactly with `[LocallyIndicable G]`, so this is what node N6 supplies (modulo the subgroup
  transfer `D H ⊆ U(H)` proved inside `Submission/Work/ORBridgeLinnell/Bridge.lean`).
* `Work.ORFinal.OreFieldFrac K G φK` — Linnell's Ore-field statement (I4′b), the *second* field;
  this is **not** N6, it is owed by N7/Linnell's lemma.
* `Work.ORFinal.hughesFreeInput_of_divLoc` — node N5's envelope together with `DivLoc` and
  `OreFieldFrac` gives the bridge's `HughesFreeInput`.  The only extra input is the *torsion*
  theorem of node N4 in the form `Work.ORLocInd.torsionFree_subgroup_locallyIndicable`
  (a torsion-free subgroup of a one-relator group is locally indicable), which is why the
  `IsMulTorsionFree` of `HughesFreeInput` can be strengthened back from `DivLoc`.

The point of the split: `DivLoc`/`OreFieldFrac` replace the `IsMulTorsionFree` requirement of
`HughesFreeInput` by local indicability, which is what N4 and N6 both produce.  It is used in
`Submission/Work/ORFinal/RingDataDiv.lean` to make the semisimplicity of `D(G)` follow from the
division-ring property at a *torsion-free* (hence, by N4, locally indicable) finite-index subgroup.
-/
import Submission.Work.ORFinal.RingData
import Submission.Work.ORLocInd.Main
import Submission.Work.OROneRel.oneRelatorCombinatorics

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

universe u v

namespace Work.ORFinal

/-- **(I4) of Jaikin-Zapirain--Linton in the form of the JZLA20 engine (node N6)**: for every
locally indicable subgroup `H` of a countable group `G` and every field embedding `φK : K →+* ℂ`,
the division closure `D H` of `K[H]` in `U(G)` is a division ring. -/
def DivLoc (K : Type u) [Field K] (G : Type v) [Group G] [Countable G] (φK : K →+* ℂ) : Prop :=
  letI := Work.ORBridgeLinnell.kAlgebra (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK
  ∀ H : Subgroup G, Work.ORLocInd.Group.LocallyIndicable H →
    ∀ x : ↥(Work.ORBridgeLinnell.D (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK H),
      x ≠ 0 → IsUnit x

/-- **The division-ring property of the closure `D H` of the M1 bridge.**  `DivOn K E φK H` is
`∀ x ∈ D H, x ≠ 0 → IsUnit x`, the conclusion of `Work.ORLinnell.LinnellDatum`'s
`division_of_torsionFree` field, at the envelope `E`.  It is a *definition* so that it can occur in
a hypothesis without a `letI` in the binder. -/
def DivOn (K : Type u) [Field K] {G : Type v} [Group G]
    (E : Work.ORVonNeumann.StarRegularEnvelope G) (φK : K →+* ℂ) (H : Subgroup G) : Prop :=
  letI := Work.ORBridgeLinnell.kAlgebra E φK
  ∀ x : ↥(Work.ORBridgeLinnell.D E φK H), x ≠ 0 → IsUnit x

/-- **(I4′b) Linnell's Ore-field statement** for the division closures of the M1 bridge: for
`N ≤ Γ` with `Γ` torsion free and `Γ/N ≅ ℤ`, every element of `D Γ` is a right quotient of elements
of the subring generated by `D N` and `Γ`.  This is the second field of
`Work.ORBridgeLinnell.HughesFreeInput`, owed by node N7 (Linnell's lemma). -/
def OreFieldFrac (K : Type u) [Field K] (G : Type v) [Group G] [Countable G]
    (φK : K →+* ℂ) : Prop :=
  letI := Work.ORBridgeLinnell.kAlgebra (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK
  ∀ (N Γ : Subgroup G), N ≤ Γ → IsMulTorsionFree Γ → Work.ORLinnell.IsExtensionByZ N Γ →
    ∀ e ∈ (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.D (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK Γ :
        Set (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G).U),
      ∃ a ∈ Subring.closure
          (((Work.ORBridgeLinnell.D (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK N :
              Subring (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G).U) :
            Set (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G).U) ∪
          Set.range (fun γ : Γ =>
            (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.gen (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) (γ : G) :
              (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G).U))),
        ∃ t ∈ Subring.closure
          (((Work.ORBridgeLinnell.D (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK N :
              Subring (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G).U) :
            Set (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G).U) ∪
          Set.range (fun γ : Γ =>
            (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.gen (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) (γ : G) :
              (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G).U))),
          t ≠ 0 ∧ e * t = a

/-- **Node N6 + node N7 + node N4 give the M1 bridge's input.**  From `DivLoc` and
`OreFieldFrac`, the `HughesFreeInput` of the M1 bridge follows for a *one-relator* group: the
stronger `IsMulTorsionFree` hypothesis of its `div_of_torsionFree` field is supplied by node N4's
`Work.ORLocInd.torsionFree_subgroup_locallyIndicable` (a torsion-free subgroup of a one-relator
group is locally indicable). -/
theorem hughesFreeInput_of_divLoc (K : Type u) [Field K] {G : Type v} [Group G] [Countable G]
    (hG : Group.OneRelator G) (φK : K →+* ℂ) (hdiv : DivLoc K G φK) (hore : OreFieldFrac K G φK) :
    Work.ORBridgeLinnell.HughesFreeInput K G (Work.ORBridgeLinnell.countableEnvelope G) φK where
  div_of_torsionFree H htf := by
    haveI htf' : IsMulTorsionFree H := htf
    have htf'' : Work.ORLocInd.IsTorsionFree H :=
      Work.ORLocInd.IsTorsionFree.of_isMulTorsionFree
    exact hdiv H (Work.ORLocInd.torsionFree_subgroup_locallyIndicable hG
      Work.OROneRel.oneRelatorCombinatorics H htf'')
  ore_field_frac := hore

end Work.ORFinal
